    "created_at": "2016-01-04T11:48:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-01-04T11:48:05Z",
    "body": "Yes, it has. And:\n1. once enabled it _stops_ redirecting, unless user explicitly allows it.\n2. if user allows redirect, the page is immediately redirected.\n3. it fails to recognize an anchor URL: if refresh content is `\"5: URL=#example\"`, Firefox, as well as IE and Edge, recalls the anchor without a page reload (Opera and Chrome reload the page instead), but it still states that the user will be redirected \"towards another page\".\n4. Firefox ignores \"refresh\" header altogether (though this is perfectly legit, as such header is non-standard, but still, every other UA honors it).\n\nAs a side note, I guess there's a need to standardise some aspects of meta refresh, particularly about internal anchors).\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
