    "created_at": "2016-09-13T10:14:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-13T10:14:52Z",
    "body": "This issue has been closed probably because I was pointed towards related resources (UAs bug report, spec standard) but I received no answer about the core proposal.\n\nAuthors could use a way to manipulate meta refresh action. As the same effect can be obtained through js, the only necessary interaction is a refresh stop mechanism (let's say by removing the element, as some authors used to believe some time ago). This would turn meta refresh into a fallback for more sophisticated solutions (e.g. prompting user to delay/stop refresh, AJAX), while keeping the low level functionality of a refreshed page in case scripts aren't usable (either for a failure or because they aren't available)\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
