    "created_at": "2016-09-13T10:35:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-13T10:35:22Z",
    "body": "The proposals in OP\n\n> 1. Why aren't UAs expected to expose at least an interface for HTTP(-equiv) \"refresh\", so that it can be read and/or blocked by a script?\n> 2. If (1) is not viable, why not simply allowing page reload to be stopped by simply removing `<meta http-equiv=\"refresh\" />`?\n\nseem fine to me (at least (2)). The problem is lack of interest from implementors. We try not to add things to the spec without knowing that it will be implemented, or (better yet) has already been implemented.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
